  - id: the_silent_lamb
    displayName: The Silent Lamb
    flavorText: Despised and rejected, the servant is brought as a lamb to the slaughter
      and opens not his mouth, wounded for transgressions and bearing the sin of
      many.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: 'A recurring figure, ''my servant,'' described across several passages
      culminating in Isaiah 52:13-53:12: one who suffers, is rejected, is silent
      before his accusers, and bears the guilt of others, then is exalted.'
    deliveredByManagerId: isaiah
    managerId: servant_of_the_lord
